INT. ABANDONED RADIO OBSERVATORY - CONTROL ROOM - NIGHT

A cathedral of dead dials. Moonlight through a cracked dish window. Four people stand around a console that has begun, impossibly, to hum.

                    ILSA
          I told you the power was cut.

                    BAYO
          It was cut. I cut it myself.

                    KESTER
          Then what's that?

                    ILSA
          A signal.

                    BAYO
          From where?

                    KESTER
          Does it matter?

                    PETRA
          It matters to me.

                    ILSA
          Petra, step back from the console.

                    PETRA
          It's saying my name.

                    BAYO
          It's static.

                    PETRA
          It's saying my name, Bayo.

                    KESTER
          Everybody, shut up and listen.

Silence. The hum deepens. Beneath it, a thin, pulsing voice rises and falls like breathing.

                    BAYO
          (whispering)
          Turn it off.

                    ILSA
          There's no switch.

                    KESTER
          Pull the plug.

                    BAYO
          There is no plug. We cut the line!

                    PETRA
          (calmly)
          It's been waiting forty years for someone to answer.

                    ILSA
          Petra, don't.

                    PETRA
          Hello?

The hum stops. Every light in the room flares white.
